_Income_Interaction\\n# Interaction term as Employed * Income.\\n# Usefulness: Captures increasing financial reliability from being employed and earning income.\\ndf[\'Employed_Income_Interaction\'] = df[\'Employed\'] * df[\'Income\']\\n\\n# Married_Log_Debt_Interaction\\n# Interaction term as Married * Log_Transformed_Debt.\\n# Usefulness: Highlights how marital status interacts with financial obligations.\\ndf[\'Married_Log_Debt_Interaction\'] = df[\'Married\'] * df[\'Log_Transformed_Debt\']\\n\\n# ZScore_Debt\\n# Z-score transformation applied to Debt.\\n# Usefulness: Normalizes Debt for interpretability and comparative analysis.\\ndf[\'ZScore_Debt\'] = (df[\'Debt\'] - df[\'Debt\'].mean()) / df[\'Debt\'].std()\\n\\n# YearsEmployed_CreditScore_Interaction\\n# Interaction term as YearsEmployed_Sqrt * CreditScore.\\n# Usefulness: Captures how employment duration amplifies creditworthiness.\\ndf[\'YearsEmployed_CreditScore_Interaction\'] = df[\'YearsEmployed_Sqrt\'] * df[\'CreditScore\']\\n\\n# Industry_LogDebt_Mean\\n# Group-wise mean of Log_Transformed_Debt by Industry.\\n# Usefulness: Encodes average industry-level financial obligations.\\ndf[\'Industry_LogDebt_Mean\'] = df.groupby(\'Industry\')[\'Log_Transformed_Debt\'].transform(\'mean\')\\n\\n# Ethnicity_CumMean_Success\\n# Cumulative success rate by Ethnicity.\\n# Usefulness: Provides a running average of credit card success rates for each ethnicity.\\ndf[\'Ethnicity_CumMean_Success\'] = df.groupby(\'Ethnicity\')[\'Success\'].cumsum() / (df.groupby(\'Ethnicity\').cumcount() + 1)\\n\\n\\n# Dropping Redundant or Unhelpful Features\\n#------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\n\\ndf.drop(columns=[\'ZipCode\'], inplace=True)\\n# ZipCode\\n# Dropped because it does not have a clear relationship with credit card application success in its current form.\\n# Usefulness: Likely to introduce noise and irrelevant to prediction outcomes.\\n\\ndf.drop(columns=[\'DriversLicense\'], inpl